1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,380
In 1814, Britain burned Washington.

2
00:00:02,850 --> 00:00:03,820
Less than a day later,

3
00:00:04,070 --> 00:00:05,400
the sky put the fire out.

4
00:00:05,582 --> 00:00:08,842
August 24th. 4,500 British troops routed

5
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:11,012
6,000 Americans at Bladensburg,

6
00:00:11,162 --> 00:00:13,662
Maryland. It's still mocked as the Bladensburg

7
00:00:13,662 --> 00:00:14,052
Races.

8
00:00:14,467 --> 00:00:16,627
That evening, they marched into the capital.

9
00:00:16,627 --> 00:00:18,377
President Madison had already fled.

10
00:00:18,615 --> 00:00:19,925
They torched the Capitol first.

11
00:00:20,435 --> 00:00:21,355
The Library of Congress,

12
00:00:21,355 --> 00:00:23,545
all 3,000 books, burned with it.

13
00:00:23,610 --> 00:00:24,910
Then up Pennsylvania Avenue,

14
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:26,160
to the President's House.

15
00:00:26,490 --> 00:00:27,720
Dinner was still on the table.

16
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:29,020
British troops ate it,

17
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:30,120
then burned the house.

18
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:31,880
They fed the fires all night.

19
00:00:32,034 --> 00:00:34,004
The next afternoon, the sky turned black.

20
00:00:34,474 --> 00:00:35,814
A violent storm hit the city,

21
00:00:35,814 --> 00:00:37,304
and the rain drowned the flames.

22
00:00:37,612 --> 00:00:39,242
A tornado tore through town,

23
00:00:39,532 --> 00:00:41,472
lifting cannons off the ground and killing

24
00:00:41,472 --> 00:00:43,382
British soldiers and civilians alike.

25
00:00:43,579 --> 00:00:46,159
Admiral Cockburn reportedly asked: "Is this

26
00:00:46,159 --> 00:00:47,399
the weather to which you are accustomed

27
00:00:47,399 --> 00:00:49,229
in this infernal country?"

28
00:00:49,548 --> 00:00:50,918
That night, the British marched out.

29
00:00:51,288 --> 00:00:53,518
The occupation lasted about 26 hours.

30
00:00:53,815 --> 00:00:55,565
So did the storm save Washington?

31
00:00:55,875 --> 00:00:58,115
Historians say no. The British came to burn,

32
00:00:58,115 --> 00:00:58,905
not to stay.

33
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:01,060
Three weeks later, the same army failed

34
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:03,520
at Baltimore, inspiring the poem that became

35
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:04,870
the Star-Spangled Banner.

36
00:01:05,133 --> 00:01:07,153
And no, the White House wasn't painted white

37
00:01:07,153 --> 00:01:08,383
to hide the scorch marks.

38
00:01:08,933 --> 00:01:10,763
It had been white since 1798.

